														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3789504">
									

<p>&quot;But he knew of course&quot;<br />
Because it's a goddamn beagle, a dog specifically bred for hunting hares(works with moles and any other hole pest too!) as a means of obtaining food and removing pests to the crops? I guess its supposed to imply cruelty, since he didn't think of eating them and instead let the dog kill them just for fun but I don't consider it a sign of a mental disorder. Maybe it has something to do with the fact my grandparents owned a beagle when I was 5-6 years old and they often told me stories of how it used to bring hares and moles back home.<br />
Otherwise it's a beautiful story of service and rehabilitation. Cold, but not cruel.</p>

